    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d560">

                <pb facs="0976" n="842" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg842"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Italy)/6–2045: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 560<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy
                    </hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caserta</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-20T19:00:00+02:00">June 20, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2695. Our 2693, June 20.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d560-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Gen Morgan just telephoned from Monf
                    aleone that agreement<anchor n="2" xml:id="d560-f2"/> with Yugos was signed at 9
                    o’clock this morning.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d560-f1" n="1" xml:id="d560-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d560-f2" n="2" xml:id="d560-f2-content">
                <p>For the text (in English and Serbo-Croatian) of the “Agreement Between the
                    Supreme Allied Commander, Mediterranean Theatre of Operations, and the Supreme
                    Commander of the Yugoslav Army” signed at Duino on June 20, 1945, and of
                    appendices C–J thereto, see Meђyнapoдни Уговори Фeдeративне Нapoдне Рeпyблиĸе
                    Jугослaвнje, 1945, No. 3 (Belgrade, Ministry of Foreign Affairs, no date). The
                    maps which comprise appendices A and B to this agreement are not printed. For
                    the “Note on Civil Administration of Zone of Venezia Giulia Coming Under Allied
                    Military Government” signed at the same time, see <ref target="#d561">document
                        No. 561</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
